.TH SDL_ShowFileDialogWithProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ShowFileDialogWithProperties \- Create and launch a file dialog with the specified properties.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_dialog.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_ShowFileDialogWithProperties(SDL_FileDialogType type, SDL_DialogFileCallback callback, void *userdata, SDL_PropertiesID props);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the supported properties:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_FILTERS_POINTER :
a pointer to a list of
.BR SDL_DialogFileFilter
structs, which will be used as filters for file-based selections\[char46] Ignored if the dialog is an \(dqOpen Folder\(dq dialog\[char46] If non-NULL, the array of filters must remain valid at least until the callback is invoked\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_NFILTERS_NUMBER :
the number of filters in the array of filters, if it exists\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_WINDOW_POINTER :
the window that the dialog should be modal for\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_LOCATION_STRING :
the default folder or file to start the dialog at\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_MANY_BOOLEAN :
true to allow the user to select more than one entry\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_TITLE_STRING :
the title for the dialog\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_ACCEPT_STRING :
the label that the accept button should have\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_FILE_DIALOG_CANCEL_STRING :
the label that the cancel button should have\[char46]
.PP
Note that each platform may or may not support any of the properties\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I type
the type of file dialog\[char46]
.TP
.I callback
a function pointer to be invoked when the user selects a file and accepts, or cancels the dialog, or an error occurs\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
an optional pointer to pass extra data to the callback when it will be invoked\[char46]
.TP
.I props
the properties to use\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called only from the main thread\[char46] The callback may be invoked from the same thread or from a different one, depending on the OS\(aqs constraints\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

